NAME
       pvmove - move data from one physical volume to others

SYNOPSIS
       pvmove SOURCE-PV [DESTINATION-PV...]

DESCRIPTION
       pvmove moves the extents in use on SOURCE-PV to other PVs of the same
       volume group (all of them, or only the ones named), while the logical
       volumes stay online. It prints its progress as a percentage. The VG
       needs enough free extents on the other PVs.

       Use it to empty a disk before taking it out of a VG with vgreduce.

EXAMPLES
       Empty /dev/vdb1 onto /dev/vdc1, then remove it from the VG:

           pvmove /dev/vdb1 /dev/vdc1
           vgreduce vgdata /dev/vdb1

SEE ALSO
       vgreduce(8), pvremove(8), pvs(8), lvm(8)
